.TH PVE-TOOLBOX 1 "@DATE@" "pve-toolbox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pve-toolbox \- modular administration toolbox for Proxmox VE hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve-toolbox
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ module ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve-toolbox
discovers self-contained administration modules and provides interactive,
full-screen, and command-line interfaces for installing, updating, checking,
reporting, and removing them.
.SH COMMANDS
@COMMANDS@
.SH OPTIONS
@OPTIONS@
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, 1 an operational failure, 2 a warning, 64 invalid input,
69 a report whose meaningful checks are unsupported, and 130 a cancelled LXC
package-update run.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables colour unless \-\-color=always is given.
.TP
.B TOOLBOX_COLOR
Colour mode when \-\-color is not given: auto (default), always, or never;
overrides NO_COLOR. auto colours a stream only when it is a terminal, unless
NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb turn it off; always/never override both. The launcher
sets this from \-\-color once and exports it, so a standalone runner reaches
the same decision.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pve-toolbox/
Runtime-generated module configuration and secrets.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pve-toolbox/
Runtime-generated module state.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/pve-toolbox/
Packaged libraries and modules.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://quwisky.github.io/pve-toolbox/
